## The lighthouse gallery

::bg{location="lighthouse_gallery" time="night"}
::music{playback="start" mood="tender" volume="down"}
::actor{character="theo" anchor="left" action="slideInLeft"}
::set{run.seen.theo = run.day}
@theo{code="0010" emotion="surprised"}: You came. You actually — okay. Okay. Look down. Don't look at me, look down.
::vfx{type="dawn"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Below the rail, every wave that breaks on the rocks breaks blue. Not moonlight blue. Blue like something alive is switching on.
@sol{code="0010"}: What is it?
@theo{code="0020"}: Tiny things. Plankton. They light up when they're scared.
@theo{code="0030" emotion="shy"}: My dad used to say it's the sea blushing.
::assert{confided(theo)}

<branch id="glow" prompt="The water flares, fades, flares.">
  <choice id="blush" text="“Then it's blushing a lot tonight.”">
    ::set{run.aff.theo += 2}
    @theo{code="0040" emotion="shy"}: …Yeah. It is.
  </choice>
  <choice id="quiet" text="Say nothing. Watch.">
    ::set{run.aff.theo += 1}
    @narrator{code="0020"}: You watch until the tide turns and the glow goes out, one wave at a time.
  </choice>
</branch>

::actor{character="theo" action="fadeOut"}
::music{playback="fadeOut"}
